1486:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Based on http://www.hyperelliptic.org/EFD/g1p/auto-shortw-jacobian.html#doubling-dbl-1998-cmo-2 
1487:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1488:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * We follow the variable naming fairly closely. The formula variations that trade a MUL for a SQR
1489:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * (plus a few ADDs) aren't useful as our bignum implementation doesn't distinguish squaring.
1490:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1491:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Standard optimizations are applied when curve parameter A is one of { 0, -3 }.
1492:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1493:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Cost: 1D := 3M + 4S          (A ==  0)
1494:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *             4M + 4S          (A == -3)
1495:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *             3M + 6S + 1a     otherwise
1496:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  */
1497:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c **** static int ecp_double_jac(const mbedtls_ecp_group *grp, mbedtls_ecp_point *R,
