1818:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c **** /*
1819:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Precompute points for the adapted comb method
1820:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1821:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Assumption: T must be able to hold 2^{w - 1} elements.
1822:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1823:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Operation: If i = i_{w-1} ... i_1 is the binary representation of i,
1824:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *            sets T[i] = i_{w-1} 2^{(w-1)d} P + ... + i_1 2^d P + P.
1825:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1826:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Cost: d(w-1) D + (2^{w-1} - 1) A + 1 N(w-1) + 1 N(2^{w-1} - 1)
ARM GAS  C:\Users\nicx5\AppData\Local\Temp\ccQL5QWa.s 			page 51


1827:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1828:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Note: Even comb values (those where P would be omitted from the
1829:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *       sum defining T[i] above) are not needed in our adaption
1830:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *       the comb method. See ecp_comb_recode_core().
1831:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1832:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * This function currently works in four steps:
1833:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * (1) [dbl]      Computation of intermediate T[i] for 2-power values of i
1834:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * (2) [norm_dbl] Normalization of coordinates of these T[i]
1835:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * (3) [add]      Computation of all T[i]
1836:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * (4) [norm_add] Normalization of all T[i]
1837:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1838:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Step 1 can be interrupted but not the others; together with the final
1839:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * coordinate normalization they are the largest steps done at once, depending
1840:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * on the window size. Here are operation counts for P-256:
1841:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1842:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * step     (2)     (3)     (4)
1843:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * w = 5    142     165     208
1844:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * w = 4    136      77     160
1845:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * w = 3    130      33     136
1846:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * w = 2    124      11     124
1847:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
1848:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * So if ECC operations are blocking for too long even with a low max_ops
1849:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * value, it's useful to set MBEDTLS_ECP_WINDOW_SIZE to a lower value in order
1850:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * to minimize maximum blocking time.
1851:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  */
